Z||000005||Voytek||08-27-2001||02:44 PM||||If all else works, it sounds like you have a leak.  First, definitely check (or have someone check) the pressure in your system.  Any A/C shop should be able to do that. If you have no pressure, get an a/c shop to do a leak test - they're fairly inexpensive.<P>I'd suggest doing the repairs yourself, if yo can.  A/C can be quite expensive to fix and there are A LOT of crooked shops in this business - they'll milk you for all you've got.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Carrolles||08-27-2001||06:03 PM||||Since the compressor does come on you have some residual pressure in the system (or someone has jumpered out the low pressure switch).  When it is running feel the connections to the drier canister (the silver can under the front hood near the windshield washer reservoir) to see if it is cold.  Unscrew tht cap from the fitting on the canister and quickly depress the shraeder valve (looks like a tire stem valve) pin to see if anything comes out.  I know this will possibly let a little CFC out into the atmosphere and cause a blackhole in the ozone layer over the north pole but do it anyway.  If you hear/feel freon escaping then you are probably low on freon charge.  If you are low this means there is a leak somewhere.  Most slow leaks are in the shraeder valve itself.  You can buy new caps for the valve that are made of metal and have o-rings for sealing leaky valves.  Another likely leak spot is the compressor seal.<P>You'll need to top off the freon charge.  This isn't cheap if you are still using R-12.  This is a good candidate for an R-134 conversion which can be done with a kit from WalMart for under $50.00.  I've done four of my cars through the years with good results.  Many on this forum don't like these kits, but to each his own.<P>Good luck,<P>carroll||||reg||1
Z||000007||cadaver||08-28-2001||12:49 AM||||Is it the complressor coming on or are you hearing the fans come on as they also come on when a/c is selected. If it is low on freon dont just top it. There is a leak as the stuff just doesnt go away it has to leak out. And do a pressure test to find the leak not a vacumm test.||||reg||1
